Closed loop transfer functions
Some standard closed loop transfer function are derived based on the image provided above.
Sensitivity: \[\begin{equation}
S=\frac{e}{r} = \frac{u}{d} = \frac{1}{1+HC}
\end{equation}\]
Complementary sensitivity: \[\begin{equation}
T=\frac{y}{r} = \frac{y}{\eta} = \frac{HC}{1+HC}
\end{equation}\]
Process sensitivity: \[\begin{equation}
HS = \frac{y}{d}=\frac{H}{1+HC}
\end{equation}\]
Control Sensitivity: \[\begin{equation}
    CS=\frac{u}{r}=\frac{C}{1+HC}
\end{equation}\]
So the general goal is to minimize the error \(e=0\) -&gt; minimizing $SS and tracking the input \(y=r\) -&gt; \(T\approx1\). This is both achieved when \(HC\) is maximized. this is called high-gain feedback.
